// Native special forms: eval.cpp. Authoring tokens: SpliceRuntime.cpp.
{"begin", "(begin expression ...)", "Evaluates expressions in order in the current frame and returns the last result; an empty begin returns void. Wrap multiple module definitions in one begin."},
{"define", "(define $name expression)", "Evaluates expression and adds a binding in the current frame. Example: (define $enabled false). Event handlers bind reserved symbols: (define Trigger (lambda ($self) true)). Frames have a native limit of 64 bindings."},
{"set!", "(set! $name expression)", "Changes an existing binding found through frame lookup. It does not create a new variable; define it first. Example: (set! $enabled true)."},
{"lambda", "(lambda ($argument ...) expression ...)", "Creates a procedure closing over its defining frame. The body runs when called and returns its last result. Event dispatch supplies the receiving object as the first argument, conventionally named $self. $self is not a magic global variable."},
{"if", "(if test when-true [when-false])", "Evaluates test and only the chosen branch. Native RefEvalIf tests its Boolean payload for exactly 1, unlike and/or. Use a Boolean comparison or predicate as the test. An omitted false branch returns void."},
{"or", "(or expression ...)", "Evaluates left to right until a result is not Boolean false, returning that value. Only Boolean false is false; numeric zero and null objects count as true here. Empty or returns false."},
{"and", "(and expression ...)", "Evaluates left to right until Boolean false, otherwise returns the last value. Only Boolean false stops evaluation. Empty and returns true."},
{"cond", "(cond (test body ...) ... (else body ...))", "Evaluates tests in order and runs the first clause whose test is not Boolean false. else is the fallback clause. Returns the last body result, or void if nothing matches."},
{"case", "(case value ((literal ...) body ...) ... (else body ...))", "Evaluates value once and compares it to unevaluated clause literals using eqv?. Example: (case $mode ((1 2) true) (else false)). Float and compound equality restrictions apply."},
{"else", "(cond ... (else expression ...))", "Marks the fallback clause in cond or case. It is not an independently callable function."},
{"let", "(let (($name value) ...) expression ...)", "Evaluates initializers in the outer frame, creates local bindings in a new frame, then evaluates the body. Initializers cannot use another binding from the same let. Example: (let (($x 2)) (+ $x 1))."},
{"while", "(while test body)", "Repeats one body expression while the test is not Boolean false. Use begin for multiple body expressions. Returns void. Ensure the condition can become false; there is no implicit yield."},
{"quote", "(quote expression)", "Returns expression data without evaluating it. Example: (quote $name) returns the symbol rather than its binding. Use explicit quote; apostrophe shorthand is not supported by the editor parser."},
{"import", "(import module-index)", "Attaches another module's frame as an import parent. Use a literal signed integer module index, not an OID or CID. Native frames allow four parent links; imported state is shared."},
{"assert", "(assert test)", "Evaluates a check and returns void. The supplied native implementation prints a failure prefix for false Boolean or numeric zero; it does not abort execution or replace validation."},
{"define-macro / define-macro-lambda", "define-macro ; define-macro-lambda", "Serialized keyword tags are preserved by the editor, but ProjectCane's evaluator has no macro-definition special-form branch. Do not author executable macros with these tokens."},
{"dot / pipe", "(lambda ($first pipe $remaining) body)", "pipe is the native lambda rest-argument marker; following extra arguments are packaged as a list for the next formal. Use it for ordinary procedure calls; event dispatch binds ordinary symbol formals positionally and does not process pipe. dot is a preserved keyword tag, not Scheme dotted-list shorthand."},
{"calls", "(procedure argument ...) ; ((geto object MethodName) argument ...)", "Evaluates a callable and its required operands. The native argument buffer has 32 slots. Fixed-arity built-ins ignore surplus operands; do not rely on surplus side effects. Reference notation [optional] and ... must be replaced with real expressions."},
{"comments / whitespace", "; comment to end of line", "Spaces and line breaks separate tokens. Semicolon comments end at the next line. One root expression is allowed per module; use begin to group definitions. Parentheses must balance."},
{"Boolean / integer / float", "true ; false ; 125 ; -1 ; 1.0 ; 1e-3", "Booleans, signed 32-bit integers and finite floating-point literals are distinct tags. Include a decimal point or exponent for a float. IDs are not automatically object pointers."},
{"$local / sym#N", "$enabled ; sym#2", "Friendly $names allocate module symbol IDs; repeated names share an ID. Use letters/underscore first, then letters/digits/underscore. sym#N explicitly preserves a numeric symbol ID; reserved event symbols are shared with the game. Do not use a local symbol's numeric ID as an EOPID."},
{"event names", "(define Trigger (lambda ($self) true))", "Single-token reserved event names such as Trigger may replace sym#2. Names containing spaces use sym#N in source. Defining a handler does not cause an event; the target's native class must dispatch it."},
{"@object aliases", "@Door ; @{Door With Spaces}", "Finds a uniquely named editor object and emits native find-object/OID/null-basis nodes. In braces, escape a closing brace or backslash with a backslash. Names must be unique; duplicate runtime OIDs still depend on hierarchy/PROXY context."},
{"property names", "(seto! @Door ALO.Hidden true) ; (geto @Door ALO.Frozen)", "Qualified CID.Property tokens compile to the same integer EOPID as raw numbers. Copy exact names from Object Operations Reference. Unqualified unique names also work; ambiguous shorthand may use the selected object's CID. Reserved language/built-in/event words retain their original meaning, so qualify properties with those names."},
{"native methods", "((geto @Destination WARP.Triggerwarp))", "geto returns a method for method descriptors. The outer parentheses call it. Pass its required arguments after geto's closing parenthesis. A method is not a seto! property write. Query methods can return values; actions can have gameplay side effects."},
{"custom options", "(ensureo $self 1173 0) ; (geto $self 1173)", "Sidebag options store custom object state. ProjectCane's geto/seto! boundary is 1173, even though BuildEopids contains descriptors through 1178. IDs at/above 1173 use sidebag behavior through these built-ins."},
{"compound payload literals", "vector#[0,0,1] ; lm#[0,1] ; clq#[0,1,0] ; smp#[1,2,3]", "Editor payload syntax preserves native typed constants without adding a constructor call. Use exactly 3 vector, 2 LM, 3 CLQ or 3 SMP finite comma-separated numbers; do not insert token-separating spaces. matrix#[...] requires exactly 16 numbers in native stored order."},
{"object#0", "object#0", "Represents a null BASIC pointer, not OID zero. Nonzero raw object pointers are not portable and are rejected. Use @aliases or find-object for real objects."},
{"void / raw tags", "void ; tag#0:0 ; tag#31:0 ; tag#33:0 ; tag#35:0", "void is the no-result value. tag#0:0 is None/null basis, tag#31:0 is a null procedure, tag#33:0 is a null method and tag#35:0 is Err. Raw payload tokens preserve tags; they are not function calls. These do not encode Nil, object IDs or new callable definitions. Prefer the dedicated syntax for ordinary values."},
